# QR codes

`\{% qr /%}` renders a QR code from `value` — a URL, a document number, or any
text. `size` (points, default 72) sets the square's side, `ecl` the
error-correction level (`low` | `medium` | `quartile` | `high`), `color` /
`background` the module / field colours, `quiet_zone` the margin (in modules,
default 4), and `align` (`left` | `center` | `right`) the placement. It is
drawn as vector, so it stays crisp at any size.

## A document number

Encode a document number so production can scan the printed guide when
packing. `value` reads straight from frontmatter — `documentNumber: 600123`
here becomes the code:

{% qr value=$markdoc.frontmatter.documentNumber size=64 /%}

For a code alone on the final page, precede it with `\{% pagebreak /%}`.

## A URL, centered and robust

Higher error correction (`ecl="high"`) tolerates smudging and folds — worth it
for print. Centered on the page:

{% qr value="https://docs.example.com/manuals/600123" size=120 ecl="high" align="center" /%}

## Tinted

`color` and `background` theme the code; keep the contrast high so it still
scans:

{% qr value="PACK-600123" size=64 color="#1b3a5b" /%}
